---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProductSpec from '@/components/ProductSpec.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Auftragstaktik | Ray Weiss"
  description="Auftragstaktik. A tactical OSINT command terminal with live frontlines, aircraft and ship tracking, air-defense envelopes, and auto-translated intel, in NATO symbology."
>
  <main class="doc">
    <div class="doc__frame">
      <header class="page-heading">
        <h1>Auftragstaktik</h1>
        <p class="dek">
          A tactical OSINT command terminal. Frontlines, aircraft, ships, air defenses, nuclear
          sites, and conflict events on one map, in NATO symbology.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-body">
        <p>
          Eight togglable map layers across four theaters. Click any marker for detail panels and
          Wikipedia links. Dark or light basemap. Export the intelligence feed as JSON, CSV, or PDF.
          Historical mode replays 140,000+ archived conflict events from 1989 to 2023 with a
          year-gradient scrubbable timeline.
        </p>
        <p>
          The name is the German doctrine of mission-type tactics: give the objective, let
          subordinates execute. Ray gave Claude Code the objective and shipped the result in about
          two weeks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable table" tabindex="0">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th
                  >Layer</th
                >
                <th
                  >What it shows</th
                >
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Tactical map</td>
                <td>
                  Nine togglable layers: frontlines, aircraft, ships, air defense, installations,
                  radar, nuclear, conflict events, density heatmap.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Intelligence feed</td>
                <td>
                  GeoConfirmed events plus auto-translated Telegram posts. Filter by source or
                  severity, click to fly the map to location.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Briefing generator</td>
                <td>
                  Local LLM (Ollama) produces structured SITREPs with location summaries, faction
                  breakdown, equipment losses, source attribution. Exports to PDF. Zero API cost.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Air defense</td>
                <td>
                  OSINT-confirmed SAM and AD installations with engagement envelopes. S-400 at 400
                  km, Patriot at 160 km, Iron Dome at 70 km.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Installations</td>
                <td>
                  Thirty-five military bases, naval ports, HQs, logistics hubs, and chokepoints
                  (Hormuz, Bab el-Mandeb, Suez, Malacca) across four theaters. Friendly or hostile
                  affiliation marked.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Radar</td>
                <td>
                  Twenty radar sites from Voronezh early warning (6,000 km range) down to coastal
                  surveillance. Purple range rings show detection and tracking envelopes.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Nuclear / CBRN</td>
                <td>
                  Known reactors, enrichment plants, weapons storage, and test sites. Yellow
                  exclusion zones. CBRN keywords in events auto-escalate to critical severity.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Historical mode</td>
                <td>
                  140,000+ archived events from UCDP GED, 1989 to 2023, across five theaters
                  (Yugoslav Wars, Gulf War, Iraq War, Afghanistan, Syrian Civil War). Cumulative
                  playback with fatality-scaled markers.
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-body terminal-section">
        <h2>Data sources</h2>
        <p>
          All public OSINT. No paid APIs required. DeepState for frontlines, GeoConfirmed for
          verified events, adsb.lol for ADS-B aircraft, aisstream.io for AIS ships, Telegram
          channels (Rybar, DeepState UA, WarGonzo) auto-translated, UCDP GED for historical events.
        </p>

        <ProductSpec heading="Stack"
          ><p>
            Next.js 15, TypeScript 5.7, MapLibre GL for the map, Ollama for local LLM briefings.
            Public repo at <a href="https://github.com/lerugray/auftragstaktik"
              >github.com/lerugray/auftragstaktik</a
            >, MIT licensed.
          </p></ProductSpec
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
